+### 12.3.4 Known associated format-lock body failures (R07-C D-F)
+
+For `env.llm_critical_deps_pinned` only, distinguish a known failed attempt to
+capture a supported format-lock body from a successful parse whose captured
+package set omits a name. Supported basenames remain exactly `uv.lock`,
+`poetry.lock`, `Pipfile.lock` and `conda-lock.yml`. The internal `Lockfile.read_issue`
+is `unreadable` when the existing safe `RepoScanner.read_text` returns None, or
+`invalid_syntax` when the corresponding TOML/JSON/YAML decoder raises its existing
+caught decode-error class. These are fixed reason codes, never raw exception text.
+The optional internal field defaults to None for legacy/manual values. None means
+no recorded failure of these two kinds; it is not a certificate of complete grammar,
+valid versions, exact builds, or successful installation. It adds no persisted field.
+
+The existing read boundary and budgets remain in force. Read failures include
+existing refusals for unsafe paths, binary, oversize, missing or inaccessible
+content. Do not inspect rejected content, retry reads, or infer a package name from
+raw failed text. A captured lock artifact remains in the existing presence inventory
+with its existing captured package set; failure does not qualify it as pin credit.
+
+Use the existing R06-B origin association from §12.2 BEFORE testing package-set
+membership. A captured declaration has an eligible format-lock origin only when
+its qualifying manager manifest is in the same logical directory as that lock
+and supports that lock format. A captured import has an eligible origin only
+through its existing nearest qualifying project root, same-manager pair, and
+existing uncertain-directory barrier. Resolve only the existing captured origins;
+do not invent an omitted import or workspace parent-lock delegation. A lock entry
+is not itself a use origin. This shared association must yield exactly the previous
+qualified-lock package credit when intersected with captured package membership.
+
+Preserve the current canonical in-use set and existing exact-declaration and
+qualified-lock credit first. For each remaining package, if at least one eligible
+associated captured format lock has either recorded read_issue, emit one
+SKIPPED/INFO instead of the used-but-unpinned FAIL/WARNING. This condition is
+independent of primary-Python coverage, including complete or zero-candidate
+views. Evaluate it before §12.3.3 when both policies could apply. Otherwise retain
+§12.3.3 and all remaining existing behavior.
+
+The new finding retains rule ID, aliases, category, audit level and existing
+display-name mapping. Use this exact message:
+
+```text
+{display} is used; an associated format lock could not be read or parsed, so missing pin evidence is not established
+```
+
+Use this exact fix hint:
+
+```text
+Review {display} declarations and associated format-lock files; restore readable, valid lock contents before deciding that exact pin evidence is absent.
+```
+
+Evidence first retains the existing first declaration for that canonical package,
+or otherwise its first captured import. Append one `kind: file` item for each
+distinct eligible associated format-lock logical path with a recorded failure,
+sorted lexicographically, with exact note
+`{display} associated; lock package contents unverified`. Other evidence defaults,
+finding origin/suppression fields, canonical package iteration and final engine
+sort remain unchanged. No extra aggregate finding or per-package PASS is added.
+
+This is bounded uncertainty about package membership relative to fixed captured
+origins and existing manager boundaries. Restoring a failed eligible lock body
+could reveal the package and supply existing credit, so its absence was not
+established. No credit is granted by the new SKIP. Unpaired, wrong-manager,
+nearer-project or barrier-blocked failed locks do not trigger this policy solely
+because they exist elsewhere in the repository. An exact declaration or another
+qualified lock still wins even when a different associated lock failed.
+
+Successful empty and successful nonmember lock bodies retain existing behavior.
+Wrong top-level shapes, invalid collections or entries, partial package extraction,
+unsupported grammar that does not raise the caught decoder error, missing candidates,
+dependency-manifest/requirements failures and omitted import origins remain outside
+this continuation. They are not silently certified by read_issue=None. Independent
+listing, dependency reading/grammar, README/config/framework completeness and broader
+sufficient certificates remain OPEN R07-C work.
+
+Mixed SKIPPED and unchanged WARNING findings are preserved. Existing empty-result
+Python veto, no-critical-package applicability skip, default rule severity and
+all other rules are unchanged. FAIL-only severity overrides do not promote the
+new SKIPPED/INFO; suppression still applies to all statuses. An isolated warning
+or promoted critical failure can stop triggering exit 1; threshold values and
+FAIL-only counting are unchanged. Default text can show Findings: PASS with a
+skipped count, while default export omits skipped counts and the old notable
+warning; full JSON retains the new finding. No renderer, schema, rule ID,
+historical report, gold answer or version is changed. This policy does not close
+the whole R07-C task.
 
